 %20browser%20for%203%20days%20before%20we%20caught%20it.\n\n━━━ Thread co
 mplet (relis avant\, paste #2-#5 en replies) ━━━\n\n1/ A Svelte 5 PR leak
 ed our Stripe key to the browser for 3 days before we caught it.\n\nThe l
 ine:\n\n  import { STRIPE_SECRET } from '$env/static/private'\n\nIn a .sv
 elte file. Generic AI reviewer approved. Green CI. Merged.\n\n2/ Why gene
 ric reviewers miss this:\n\nThey parse .svelte like .js. They see "valid 
 import\, valid fetch\, ship it."\n\nBut $env/static/private in a CLIENT c
 omponent = the secret ends up in your browser bundle. Devtools-readable. 
 Public.\n\n3/ Same category of misses I kept finding:\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
