SUMMARY:🌍 [W1] Post X thread EN — i18n Autopilot
DESCRIPTION:Clique pour tweet #1 (prérempli) :\nhttps://twitter.com/inten
 t/tweet?text=A%20French%20user%20emailed%20me%3A%20%22Half%20your%20setti
 ngs%20page%20is%20in%20English.%20Is%20that%20normal%3F%22\n\n━━━ Thread 
 complet (relis avant\, paste #2-#5 en replies) ━━━\n\n1/ A French user em
 ailed me: "Half your settings page is in English. Is that normal?"\n\nI h
 ad shipped a new settings page 3 weeks earlier. en.json updated. fr.json\
 , forgotten. de.json\, forgotten. Every non-English user saw raw keys or 
 English fallback. For 3 weeks. Nobody flagged it. The PR was green.\n\n2/
  It's the silent class of bug. en works. The other languages just rot.\n\
 nManual translation is the trap that creates it. Engineers update the sou
 rce language because that's what they're thinking in. The translation tas
 k lives "in the next sprint." Forever.\n\n3/ So I built it as a GitHub Ac
 tion. On every PR:\n\n→ diff locale files\n→ find keys in en.json missing
  elsewhere\n→ AI-translate them\n→ preserve {name} / {{count}} / <tags> e
 xactly\n→ commit back to the branch\n\n4/ The hard part was placeholder p
 reservation:\n\n  "greeting": "Welcome\, {name}!"\n  → "Bonjour\, {nom} !
 "   ← BROKEN\n\nThe token is code\, not a word. Wrapping it as opaque\, t
 hen validating it returned intact\, is most of the engineering.\n\n5/ Fre
 e MIT GitHub Action. Works with i18next\, next-intl\, react-intl\, vue-i1
 8n\, FormatJS. Flat or nested layouts.\n\n→ github.com/marketplace/action
 s/i18n-autopilot\n\nIf you ship multilingual: how far behind are your non
 -English files right now? (Mine were 3 weeks\, hence this.)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━
 ━━━━━━\nRepo : https://github.com/marketplace/actions/i18n-autopilot
LOCATION:https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=A%20French%20user%20emaile
 d%20me%3A%20%22Half%20your%20settings%20page%20is%20in%20English.%20Is%20
 that%20normal%3F%22
CATEGORIES:AUTOPILOT-WEEKLY-I18N
