SUMMARY:🗃️ [W1] Post X thread EN — Migration Autopilot
DESCRIPTION:Clique pour tweet #1 (prérempli) :\nhttps://twitter.com/inten
 t/tweet?text=A%20migration%20that%20ran%20in%200.4%20seconds%20on%20stagi
 ng%20locked%20our%20prod%20users%20table%20for%2020%20minutes.\n\n━━━ Thr
 ead complet (relis avant\, paste #2-#5 en replies) ━━━\n\n1/ A migration 
 that ran in 0.4 seconds on staging locked our prod users table for 20 min
 utes.\n\nThe line:\n\n  ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN phone SET NOT NULL
 \;\n\nThree tokens. Staging: 30K rows. Prod: 1.2B rows. Postgres scanned 
 every row to validate. ACCESS EXCLUSIVE the whole time.\n\n2/ Staging lie
 s to you in 3 ways:\n\n- Volume: 30K vs 1.2B. Lock duration scales with r
 ows.\n- Contention: 1 dev vs 1000s of writers waiting on each row.\n- Ver
 sions: PG11 vs PG15 lock-upgrade semantics differ.\n\nThe PR review never
  surfaces "this statement will lock writes for a full table scan."\n\n3/ 
 So I built the linter. 15 rules across:\n\n- Data loss: DROP COLUMN\, DRO
 P TABLE\, TRUNCATE\n- Locks: SET NOT NULL\, ALTER COLUMN TYPE\, non-CONCU
 RRENTLY index\n- The Prisma/Drizzle trap: CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY insid
 e a wrapped tx (fails)\n- Silent breaks: FK without NOT VALID\, rename co
 lumn during deploy\n\n4/ Deterministic\, not LLM. False positives kill me
 rge-gating tools — the eval has a hard 0-FP gate on 50 cases.\n\nRule sou
 rces: Squawk\, ankane/strong_migrations\, Atlas PG301-311\, real incident
  postmortems.\n\n5/ Free MIT GitHub Action. 2-minute install\, no API key
 .\n\n→ github.com/marketplace/actions/migration-autopilot\n\nWhat's the w
 orst migration you've seen take down prod?\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nRepo : ht
 tps://github.com/marketplace/actions/migration-autopilot
LOCATION:https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=A%20migration%20that%20ran
 %20in%200.4%20seconds%20on%20staging%20locked%20our%20prod%20users%20tabl
 e%20for%2020%20minutes.
