SUMMARY:🗃️ [W2] Post X thread EN — Migration Autopilot
DESCRIPTION:Clique pour tweet #1 (prérempli) :\nhttps://twitter.com/inten
 t/tweet?text=Migration%20bug%20of%20the%20week%3A%20CREATE%20INDEX%20CONC
 URRENTLY%20inside%20Prisma%20fails%20at%20runtime.\n\n━━━ Thread complet 
 (relis avant\, paste #2-#5 en replies) ━━━\n\n1/ Migration bug of the wee
 k: CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY inside Prisma fails at runtime.\n\nYou did t
 he homework. You know plain CREATE INDEX blocks writes. So you wrote:\n\n
   CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_email ON users (email)\;\n\nBut Prisma wr
 aps migrations in a transaction. And CONCURRENTLY can't run in a transact
 ion.\n\nThe migration crashes at deploy. Half-applied. 3am wake-up.\n\n2/
  Same pattern across ORMs:\n\n- Prisma — implicit tx wrapper\n- Drizzle —
  drizzle-kit same behavior\n- Rails — needs `disable_ddl_transaction!` pe
 r-migration\n- TypeORM — same trap\n\nThe fix is documented but hidden. P
 risma needs --create-only + manual BEGIN/COMMIT removal.\n\n3/ The 2-step
  safe pattern:\n\nmigration_a.sql (in normal Prisma flow):\n  -- prep wor
 k\, schema changes\n\nmigration_b.sql (raw SQL\, no tx wrapper):\n  CREAT
 E INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_email ON users (email)\;\n\nYou have to lie to P
 risma a bit. The ORM wasn't designed for this.\n\n4/ My Action catches th
 is in PR review (rule `prisma-concurrently-in-txn`):\n\n  ❌ HIGH — CREATE
  INDEX CONCURRENTLY can't run inside Prisma's wrapped tx\n  Safe rewrite:
  split into a separate migration with the BEGIN stripped\n\nCheck fails. 
 Merge blocked.\n\n5/ Free MIT GitHub Action. Multi-ORM (Prisma/Drizzle/Ra
 ils/raw SQL):\n\n→ github.com/marketplace/actions/migration-autopilot\n\n
 What ORM-specific migration trap has bitten you?\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nRep
 o : https://github.com/marketplace/actions/migration-autopilot
LOCATION:https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Migration%20bug%20of%20the
 %20week%3A%20CREATE%20INDEX%20CONCURRENTLY%20inside%20Prisma%20fails%20at
 %20runtime.
