SUMMARY:🪄 [W3] Post X thread EN — Svelte Autopilot
DESCRIPTION:Clique pour tweet #1 (prérempli) :\nhttps://twitter.com/inten
 t/tweet?text=This%20is%20what%20a%20real%20catch%20looks%20like.\n\n━━━ T
 hread complet (relis avant\, paste #2-#5 en replies) ━━━\n\n1/ This is wh
 at a real catch looks like.\n\n[Bot PR comment screenshot]\n\nPR adds a c
 ontact form posting to SendGrid. The bot:\n\n  🔴 CRITICAL — $env/static/
 private imported in client component\n  src/routes/contact/+page.svelte:5
 \n  \n  Move SENDGRID_API_KEY to a server-only file (+page.server.ts).\n 
  Otherwise it ships in the browser bundle.\n\n2/ Check failed. Merge bloc
 ked.\n\nThe thing about secret leaks in client bundles: you don't find ou
 t from your monitoring. You find out from a security researcher emailing 
 you. Or from someone abusing the key.\n\nOr\, if you're lucky\, never. An
 d the key just sits in production for years.\n\n3/ This is rule-based\, n
 ot AI guesswork. The rule is:\n\n  IF file matches /\\.svelte$/ AND\n  fi
 le imports from /\\$env\\/(static|dynamic)\\/private/ AND\n  file is clie
 nt-reachable (not +page.server.ts):\n    flag as critical\n\n15+ such rul
 es. Each one a specific Svelte / SvelteKit footgun.\n\n4/ Free MIT. No AP
 I key. Multi-rule:\n\n- $env/static/private leak\n- top-level window/docu
 ment/localStorage (SSR crash)\n- {@html} on user input (XSS)\n- destructu
 red $state (silent reactivity loss)\n- $effect doing what $derived should
 \n\n5/ → github.com/marketplace/actions/svelte-autopilot\n\nTry it on you
 r last PR. Does it flag something real?\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nRepo : https
 ://github.com/marketplace/actions/svelte-autopilot
